nAlignment:bF(`A table row places itself by its own w:tblPrEx alignment; a trailing-aligned row ends past the text edge by its first cell's leading margin`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.60 tblPrEx`),firstRowExceptionAlignsTable:yF(`The first row's w:tblPrEx alignment aligns the whole table; later rows' alignments do not apply`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.60 tblPrEx`),floatingTableContentOrigin:bF(`A floating table with a numeric offset or a left, inside, right, or outside alignment positions its cell content, not its outer edge`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.57 tblpPr`),floatingTableBandHoldsSpaceAfter:bF(`The last line of a paragraph and its space after must both clear a floating table band; later modes test the line alone`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.57 tblpPr`),raisedFloatKeepsUnbalancedPlace:bF(`A text-anchored floating table raised above its anchor in balanced section columns keeps its place from the unbalanced layout`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.57 tblpPr`),floatingTableOverlapMovesLeft:yF(`A floating table that may not overlap moves left of the table it meets when the right side has no room`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.56 tblOverlap`),cellFloatMovedDownIndents:yF(`A floating table in a table cell that moves below an earlier one also moves right by its own left text distance`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.56 tblOverlap`),headerFooterAnchorsWrapText:yF(`Header and footer text outside tables wraps around anchored objects`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §20.4.2.3 anchor`),headerRowsKeepWithBody:yF(`Header rows keep with the opening body rows; the table starts on the next page if both do not fit`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.49 tblHeader`),justifiedSpaceShrink:yF(`Justified lines may shrink spaces to fit one more word`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.13 jc`),balancedSpaceShrink:yF(`With balanced single-byte and double-byte widths, a space at the balanced width keeps it when justified and distributed lines shrink their spaces`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.15.3.3 balanceSingleByteDoubleByteWidth`),keepNextGivesTailLines:yF(`A keep-with-next paragraph that fits whole gives its last lines to the next page with its successor`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.15 keepNext`),legacyPercentTableContentWidth:bF(`A top-level percent-width table resolves its width against the legacy content width`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.63 tblW`),legacySharedGridLineSideRules:bF(`Collapsed side rules center on shared grid lines for every simple table, in either direction; a percent width keeps the legacy reference box`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.38 tblBorders`),legacySpacedFrameRuleCenters:bF(`A spaced table aligns the centers of its outer frame rules; later modes align their outer edges`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.38 tblBorders`),modernBidiTableRuleShift:yF(`A right-to-left table sits half its mean outer side rule toward its visual left`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.1 bidiVisual`),modernGridLineSideRules:yF(`Side rules center on grid lines for covered dxa/auto shapes and one-rule percent widths; edge-aligned grids move by half a rule`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.38 tblBorders`),noteAreaHoldsLineSpacing:yF(`Auto line spacing below a body line must fit above the footnote area; legacy modes let it cross the area as it crosses a bottom margin`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.11 Footnotes and Endnotes`),noteAreaHoldsSpaceAfter:yF(`A paragraph space after must fit above the footnote area; legacy modes let a paragraph that cites no footnote cross the area as it crosses a bottom margin`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.11 Footnotes and Endnotes`),noteTableCellKeeps:yF(`Note reference bands in table rows honor cell widow control and keep-lines cuts`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.11 Footnotes and Endnotes`),openingColumnBreakTakesNoLine:bF(`A column break that opens a paragraph leaves no line in the column it ends`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.3.1 br`),inlineObjectStaysBesideFloat:bF(`An inline object that opens its line stays on it beside a float even when it is wider than the gap there, and runs past the margin or over the float. In modern modes it moves below the float`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §20.4.2.3 anchor`),leftTabStopsPastMargin:bF(`A custom left tab stop past the margin is honoured, and the text after it may run past the margin. In modern modes the stop reaches the margin and its text wraps there`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.37 tabs`),edgeStopKeepsTrailingTabs:bF(`Outside a table cell, a tab after text that ends on a custom stop at the right edge stays on that line when no stop lies past it. In modern modes, and in table cells in every mode, the tab opens the next line`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.3.32 tab`),oversizedRowKeepGroupReleases:bF(`A kept row group that exceeds a fresh page starts beside preceding content, except directly below authored headers`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.15 keepNext`),lineEndPunctuationAtEveryAlignment:bF(`Line-end East Asian punctuation hangs past the margin at every paragraph alignment, and the text before it fills the measure. The paragraph kinsoku switch does not stop it. With punctuation compression (w:characterSpacingControl), punctuation compresses to fit a line at every alignment, within half the advance of each group it admits, and Korean marks keep their advances; a hyphen-minus before a letter, digit, or symbol is no break opportunity. Modern modes hang and fit only in justified and distributed paragraphs`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.21 overflowPunct`),koreanHangingLineFills:yF(`A Korean paragraph-final mark that hangs past the margin lets the text before it fill the measure. Earlier modes keep that last line at its natural width`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.21 overflowPunct`),largestWrapTieLeft:yF(`Square wrapping on the largest side keeps text on the physical left when both sides are equally wide; earlier modes keep it on the right`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §20.4.2.17 wrapSquare`),wrapIgnoresMultipleSpacingExtra:yF(`A wrap band moves a line only where it crosses the text or picture of the line, not the extra space an auto line-spacing multiple adds below it`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.33 spacing`),positionedTableBreaksAtMargin:yF(`A page- or margin-positioned table that breaks ends its first fragment at the bottom margin, not the page edge`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.57 tblpPr`),omittedRepeatEndsPage:yF(`Content after a table whose last page leaves out the repeated header rows starts on the next page`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.49 tblHeader`),pageBreakBeforeKeepsSpace:bF(`A paragraph with a page break before keeps its space before at the top of the new page. In modern modes only the first block of a section keeps it`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.23 pageBreakBefore`),pageBreakLinesStretch:bF(`A justified line that ends in a page or column break stretches to the measure, unless it is the last line of its paragraph`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.3.1 br`),repeatBoundaryUsesHeaderRule:bF(`A complete body row directly below a repeated header row reserves the wider of its own top border and the header row's bottom border; modern modes keep the band of the row it follows in the table`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.49 tblHeader`),repeatKeepsWholeRow:bF(`Repeated header rows stay above a row that cannot split and does not fit below them, or a row whose first line, or the first row of a nested table that opens a cell, does not fit below them, also when the row continues from the previous page; the row stays whole and runs past the bottom margin`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.49 tblHeader`),repeatedHeaderYieldsToTerminalRule:yF(`Repeated header rows are omitted when the last fixed-height row fits below them only without its bottom rule`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.49 tblHeader`),rowPageBreakYieldsToKeep:yF(`A row with a page break does not start a page when the row before it keeps with it`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.15 keepNext`),tallRowStaysWhole:bF(`A row that cannot split and is taller than a page stays whole on its page and runs past the bottom margin`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.4.6 cantSplit`),tableParagraphWidowControl:yF(`Paragraphs that split inside table cells apply widow and orphan control`,`ECMA-376 Part 1 §17.3.1.44 widowControl`),vMergeTextMovesPast